  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Tamil Nadu Food Safety And Drug ... vs Mariappan on 6 September, 2018 Author: Huluvadi G.Ramesh Bench: Huluvadi G.Ramesh, K.Kalyanasundaram",
    "facts": "2. The said Miscellaneous Petition has been filed by the respondent in W.P.No.19831/2017 to vacate the interim order of stay granted on 02.08.2017 in that writ petition. Aggrieved over the same, the present Writ Appeal has been filed. It further appears that in the meanwhile, the Government having created a new Department for implementation of the said act, decided to appoint the Food Safety Officials by deployment from the Senior Sanitary Inspector/Food Inspector working in the Municipal Corporation as well as the Food Inspector under the Health Department. The 1st respondent, being the senior, he has been so deployed along with others. The same was opposed by the appellant herein, but the 1st respondent has obtained a stay from a learned Single Judge of this Court by filing W.P.No.19831/2017 in respect of the said deployment. Therefore, the appellant, namely, the Tamil Nadu Food Safety and Drug Administration Department has filed a Vacate Stay Petition before the learned Single Judge. The same was dismissed by order dated 20.02.2018 observing as under: ''...such deployment appears to be permanent as the department having created, wants to fill up the post with Senior Food Inspector working under the repealed Food Adulteration Act.",
    "arguments": "His original employer i.e. Greater Chennai Municipal Corporation/Respondent No.3 also support such stand with the submission that no post exist to accommodate the writ petitioner.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "His original employer i.e. Greater Chennai Municipal Corporation/Respondent No.3 also support such stand with the submission that no post exist to accommodate the writ petitioner.",
